.TH LSUSD 1 "2026-05-01" "lsusd 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lsusd \- list USB serial devices with their associated USB metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsusd
.RB [ \-p | \-c | \-j ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-w ]
.br
.B lsusd
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lsusd
discovers USB serial device nodes and displays their associated USB metadata
(vendor, product, serial number, VID:PID) in a formatted table.
.PP
On macOS, discovery is performed via
.BR ioreg (8),
matching
.I /dev/cu.usbmodem*
and
.I /dev/cu.usbserial*
device nodes.
.PP
On Linux, discovery is performed via sysfs by checking every tty device
for a USB ancestor, so devices renamed via udev rules are also detected.
.PP
With
.BR \-w " / " \-\-watch ,
.B lsusd
first prints currently connected USB serial devices as
.I present
events in a live terminal table, then waits for USB serial device changes and
redraws the table. This mode is event-driven: on macOS it uses IOKit serial
service notifications, and on Linux it listens to kernel uevents through the
netlink socket. A fresh snapshot is taken only after an event arrives, in order
to compute add/remove rows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-plain
Plain tab\-separated output without headers or box drawing.
Suitable for consumption by
.BR cut (1),
.BR awk (1),
or shell scripts.
The columns are: device, product, vendor, serial, vidpid.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-csv
CSV output with a header row.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
JSON array output.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-spinner
Disable the progress spinner shown during device discovery.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
Show current USB serial devices in a live table, then watch changes until
interrupted.
With
.BR \-j ,
events are emitted as newline-delimited JSON objects. With
.BR \-c ,
the columns are: action, device, product, vendor, serial, vidpid. With
.BR \-p ,
the same columns are emitted as tab-separated text without a header.
The action is
.IR present ,
.IR add ,
or
.IR remove .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (devices found or no devices found).
.TP
.B 1
Unsupported platform.
.SH EXAMPLES
List all USB serial devices in the default table format:
.PP
.RS
.B lsusd
.RE
.PP
Get plain output for scripting:
.PP
.RS
.B lsusd \-p | cut \-f1
.RE
.PP
Export as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.B lsusd \-j > devices.json
.RE
.PP
Watch for USB serial add/remove events:
.PP
.RS
.B lsusd \-\-watch
.RE
.SH AUTHORS
Dr.\& Michael Lauer
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ioreg (8),
.BR system_profiler (8)
